// Plugin: no-raw-id — a Zod `*Id` field typed as a raw `z.string()` chain.
// Use `brandedId<T>()` (nanoid) or `typeIdSchema(ID_PREFIX.x)` (TypeID) from `@orb/kit/ids`.
// The brand flows through the contract → service → client, so swapping a ChatId for a CharacterId
// becomes a tsc error instead of silent FK drift. Skips values already using a brand helper.
// Suppress: // biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-raw-id: polymorphic ref
// Refs: Spine-TypeScript-and-Patterns.md §1, Spine-TypeScript-and-Patterns.md.
language js

`$key: $val` as $prop where {
  $key <: r".*Id$",
  $val <: contains `z.string()`,
  $val <: not contains `brandedId`,
  $val <: not contains `typeIdSchema`,
  $val <: not contains `castId`,
  register_diagnostic(span=$prop, message="id field typed as a raw z.string() — use brandedId<T>() (nanoid) or typeIdSchema(ID_PREFIX.x) (TypeID) from @orb/kit/ids. The brand flows through the contract surface into services + client, so swapping a ChatId for a CharacterId becomes a type error instead of silent FK drift. See Spine-TypeScript-and-Patterns.md.")
}
